# ── Build outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────
*.exe
*.o
# NOT a blanket `*.obj`: the Wavefront 3D models under assets/
# (terrain.obj, water.obj, cube.obj) share that extension and are project
# CONTENT, not compiler output. Blanket-ignoring them kept every model out of
# the repository, so a fresh clone ran the fps demo with no terrain, water or
# cube at all. `language/build/` and `_temp/` already exclude every real
# compiler object, so the two lines below split the extension by PURPOSE: the
# general rule still catches stray objects, the negation keeps the assets.
*.obj
!**/assets/*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dylib
*.out
nul
todo.md
# ...but the icon theme's plan is part of the theme, not a scratch note.
!dotfile/ICON_THEME/TODO.md
_temp/
language/tests/*

!language/tests/
# Build output. Every makefile.py in this repository writes its product under
# _temp/ (already ignored above), so nothing here should ever be produced in the
# tree again. The entries below are the OLD output locations plus the generated
# sources that used to be written into language/_SRC/: they are listed so that a
# tree which still has them - or a stale build run - cannot dirty the working
# directory and block `git pull` with "merge first".
language/build/
language/_SRC/embed_freemono.c
language/_SRC/embed_icon.c
gnuchan_softwares/gcl_WM/build/
gnuchan_softwares/gcl_DM/build/
# ── GCL test temp files (_NOTES/) ──────────────────────────
language/_NOTES/t_*.gcsf
language/_NOTES/t_*.gcsf.c
# ── Python embeddable (downloaded, not source) ─────────────
*.pyd
*.zip
*.cat
*.pth
# ── OS / IDE garbage ──────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
# ── Python cache ──────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
wwww
export.py
# ── GnuchanOS live ISO (distro/) ──────────────────────────
# distro/_build is where build.sh writes: the working copy of the live-build
# tree, the chroot and binary trees, and the finished .iso. None of it is
# source and all of it is large.
distro/_build/
# auto/config copies the source trees into the overlay before the build, so
# that live-build can copy them into the image. That copy is build output and
# is regenerated on every run; the authored configuration is beside it under
# config/, which IS tracked.
distro/config/includes.chroot/opt/gnuchanos/
